Regression (PRE-EXISTING, unrelated to NEARS-2543 diff): logging out FROM the
Profile screen (the only screen with the Logout button) leaves the screen
stuck on an infinite CircularProgressIndicator instead of returning to a
usable guest Profile view. Reproduced twice, with two different accounts
(customer@nears.com and qa.singlestore@nears.com), on emulator-5558.

Root cause (read, not just grepped): UserApp/lib/features/profile/screens/profile_screen.dart
line ~92-101 — `bool isLoggedIn = AuthHelper.isLoggedIn();` is computed once
in the OUTER State.build() and closed over inside
`GetBuilder<ProfileController>(builder: (profileController) => (isLoggedIn &&
profileController.userInfoModel == null) ? CircularProgressIndicator() : ...)`.
MenuController.logout() -> ProfileController.clearUserInfo() nulls
userInfoModel and calls update(), which rebuilds ONLY the inner GetBuilder —
not the outer State.build() — so the closure's `isLoggedIn` stays stale=true
from before logout while userInfoModel is now null, and the ternary shows the
spinner forever (nothing re-fetches userInfo because the user is actually
logged out). Confirmed by: pressing system Back exits the stuck screen to
Home in a correct clean guest state; re-entering Profile fresh renders the
correct "Guest User / Login" view immediately (proves the underlying
clearSharedData()/logout data-clear is correct — only the ALREADY-MOUNTED
Profile screen's own build fails to react).

Evidence — flutter run log (UserApp), around each repro, shows the
NEARS-2543 fix behaving correctly: the invalidation POST and the guest
re-mint both land clean (no 401, no [FAIL], no refresh triggered):

[NET] POST endpoint=/api/v1/customer/cm-firebase-token
[INFO] msg="FCM registration id obtained"
[NET] POST endpoint=/api/v1/auth/guest/request
[NET] endpoint=/api/v1/customer/cm-firebase-token http_status=200
[NET] endpoint=/api/v1/auth/guest/request http_status=200

No [FAIL]/[ERR] lines correlate with either repro. This is a UI-navigation
bug in profile_screen.dart / menu_controller.dart — neither file is touched
by the NEARS-2543 diff (UserApp/lib/api/api_client.dart +
UserApp/lib/features/auth/domain/repositories/auth_repository.dart only) —
so it predates this fix and is filed as a regression_bug, not a task_bug.
Screenshot: bug-profile-screen-stuck-spinner-after-logout.png (device
emulator-5558, light mode).
